# L §6.1 What same does: a place two of them book takes it at the point of the last of them in the day's order, "and
# where they give it different amounts or days it is a hole movement there (HOLE-SAME) that may fall on either day";
# L §8.1 HOLE-SAME "<p> and <q> are one, but <x> differs on <d>: <a> (<row>) and <b> (<row>)". As
# L6_1_same_decision_waits, but the bank's row says 250.00 PLN where sweep, at its point, moves 300.00 PLN: both places
# take the hole from 2026-03-31.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
input bank: observed
input sweep_day: date

move sweep: transfers
  on sweep_day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount bal(konto)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  sweep_day = 2026-03-31 "plan"
  opening[konto] = 300.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  opening[savings] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version stmt
  cite s
  known 2026-04-02
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-31, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to savings amount 250.00 PLN) "linia 1"
  same bank[r1] = sweep

ask k: bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
ask sv: bal(savings, 2026-12-31)
=== expect
k: ?"bank[r1] and sweep are one, but the leg at konto differs on 2026-03-31: 250.00 PLN (bank[r1]) and 300.00 PLN (sweep)" (bank[r1], sweep)
  cut 2026-10-20
sv: ?"bank[r1] and sweep are one, but the leg at savings differs on 2026-03-31: 250.00 PLN (bank[r1]) and 300.00 PLN (sweep)" (bank[r1], sweep)
  cut 2026-10-20
